 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-* **Sparse Lidar Coverage:** Relying on Lidar features alone results in low-resolution rendering [S1].
-* **Limited Field of View:** Lidar does not cover the entire scene (e.g., building surfaces above a certain height), yielding blank rendering in those regions [S1]. The hybrid approach combines explicit Lidar geometry with a high-resolution implicit grid to leverage their complementary benefits [S1].
-* **Occlusion:** Depth supervision accounts for occlusion [S1].
